STATUS: Create a matched pair of low, wide chapter-map-preview thumbnails for
the campaign selector. These are miniature scenic previews, not symbolic
chapter icons. They must fit side by side on the existing shallow parchment
backplate.

## Reference images

- Attach the user-provided campaign-screen reference screenshot. Use only its
  upper-right chapter selector to match the thumbnails' compact, horizontal
  proportions and small scenic-preview treatment. Do not recreate the screen.
- Attach
  `assets_src/campaign/chapter-maps/campaign_chapter_01_green_frontier_map.png`
  as the primary terrain reference for Chapter 1.
- Attach
  `assets_src/campaign/chapter-maps/campaign_chapter_02_broken_valley_map.png`
  as the primary terrain reference for Chapter 2. Do not substitute the
  existing square crystal emblem; it is not a map preview.
- Create a readable miniature preview of each chapter's environment rather
  than inventing a detached emblem.

## Output

- Generate exactly one PNG sprite sheet:
  `campaign_chapter_thumbnails_sheet.png`.
- Save it under `assets_src/campaign/chapter-thumbnails/`.
- Canvas: exactly 1024 x 256 pixels, horizontal, opaque RGB or RGBA with a
  fully opaque alpha channel.
- Arrange exactly two equal 512 x 256 pixel cells side by side:
  1. Chapter 1 thumbnail, using Reference 1.
  2. Chapter 2 thumbnail, using Reference 2.
- Each cell is a 2:1 landscape thumbnail. Fill the cell edge to edge with
  artwork; do not leave transparent padding or add a gutter between cells.
- Design the pair to sit side by side within the existing approximately
  312 x 104 dp shared parchment panel. Leave room for live UI status badges
  without making either landscape too small.
- Keep both previews at the same scale, camera distance, detail density, and
  painterly finish so they read as a coordinated set.

## Thumbnail direction

- Show a compact, painterly miniature vista or map-preview of each chapter's
  environment. Use broad, legible terrain shapes and strong color grouping so
  the scene remains recognizable at small screen size.
- **Chapter 1 — The Green Frontier:** show the lush green frontier from
  Reference 1, using its characteristic vegetation, hills, waterways, and
  warm natural palette.
- **Chapter 2 — The Broken Valley:** match the fractured valley in the
  supplied Chapter 2 map, using its cold palette and broken terrain.
- Keep the camera angle and degree of detail consistent with the reference
  maps. A simplified overview or carefully composed map-inspired crop is
  acceptable; do not turn the scene into a single subject emblem.
- Let each image fill its wide rectangle. Keep focal terrain and important
  color contrasts away from the outermost few pixels so small UI badges can
  overlay a corner without obscuring the scene.
- Use clear, readable silhouettes and restrained details. Avoid tiny
  structures, particles, or textures that collapse into noise when reduced.
- Keep both thumbnails equally bright and complete. Do not darken Chapter 2
  to imply its locked state; selection, completion, and lock states are live UI.

## Separation from the parchment and live UI

- Generate only the two landscape thumbnails. The shared parchment is a
  separate asset and must not be baked into either cell.
- Do not add an individual card, frame, border, tab shape, ribbon, or rounded
  tile around either thumbnail. The images are placed directly on the shared
  parchment.
- Do not include chapter numbers, names, title text, letters, runes that
  resemble writing, locks, checkmarks, progress indicators, or selection
  treatments.
- Do not reproduce the whole campaign screenshot, outer map frame, Back
  control, Start Level button, HUD, or unrelated screen elements.
- Do not add captions, decorative badges, detached glow, shadows, or
  transparent margins.
- Keep any terrain or landmark detail faithful to the matching map. Do not add
  unrelated characters, enemies, weapons, or gameplay scenes.

## Review and extraction

- Confirm the output is exactly 1024 x 256 pixels and contains exactly two
  edge-to-edge 512 x 256 landscape previews in Chapter 1 / Chapter 2 order.
- Confirm each cell reads as a miniature of its chapter's environment, not as
  a symbol, crest, or square app icon.
- Confirm both thumbnails share the same camera scale and visual treatment,
  while their landscapes and palettes remain clearly distinct.
- Confirm no individual card frame, text, chapter number, lock, checkmark, or
  parchment is baked into the artwork.
- Confirm the images remain legible when displayed side by side on a shallow
  312 x 104 dp parchment panel, with room for separate live status badges.
- After approval, split the actual sprite sheet into two 512 x 256 RGBA source
  assets without changing the composition or trimming either thumbnail.
- Do not replace the currently installed square chapter-tab assets until the
  generated previews have been reviewed and approved.

## Negative prompt

symbolic icon, square icon, emblem, crest, medallion, isolated leaf, isolated
crystal, isolated object, portrait composition, tall composition, full campaign
screen, UI screenshot, button, card, individual tile, card frame, border,
parchment background, ribbon, chapter number, chapter name, title, text,
letters, writing, runes, lock, checkmark, progress bar, selection glow,
darkened locked state, badge, HUD, Back control, Start Level control, unrelated
map, mismatched camera scale, inconsistent art style, tiny unreadable detail,
noise, detached shadow, detached glow, particles, watermark, signature
